1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,540
It is more important, I feel like, than ever in my lifetime that children are not only provided information, but provided encouragement to be information seekers.

2
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:23,520
Cultivating curiosity as a character trait is one of the things that I think is going to be imperative to challenging the continual rise of willful ignorance as a method of legislation, of living, of leadership, etc.

3
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,420
It's always been there. It's always been there.

4
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,160
But now it's real like in your face.

5
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:36,620
And I would say another way that we, you know, continue to challenge willful ignorance is by not practicing it about the things that we need to be doing.

6
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:39,580
A lot of us practice willful ignorance about our role in civics.

7
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:44,620
Well, my vote doesn't matter. Well, you know that your vote matters or else they wouldn't be working so hard to make it for you not to vote.

8
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:45,920
So that's just willful ignorance, right?

